WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.192
BHW Riza notices standing water in three yards. She speaks with residents and asks what they have noticed too.

2
00:00:09.192 --> 00:00:19.920
Riza invites residents, the purok leader, and health staff to talk. Someone suggests another time; she listens before they choose a time together.

3
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:30.240
Riza records what she saw: standing water in three yards. She does not claim it caused children to become ill, because that has not been established.

4
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:42.240
With residents and health staff, she identifies who will bring the concern to the barangay planning team for health and who will report back. Confirm the actual route with the local health team.

5
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:54.096
Barangay input may inform discussion for the Local Investment Plan for Health, or LIPH. It goes through the existing local process; funding is not guaranteed.

6
00:00:54.096 --> 00:01:05.832
As a Community Organizer, Riza listens, connects people, reports what was seen rather than assumed, and follows the local process until residents receive a response.
